        "original_id": "35d531a6-0213-5575-a4ce-11296c45e2e1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Priest Rapids Dam, Hanford Site, Columbia River, Yakima County, Grant County, Washington, Yakima Firing Range, Rattlesnake Mountain\n- Organizations: Grant County Public Utility District, United States federal government\n- Projects: Wanapum Dam\n- Concepts: hydroelectric dams, nuclear production complexes\n\nFacts:\n- Priest Rapids Dam is a hydroelectric concrete gravity dam on the Columbia River in Washington, between the Yakima Firing Range and the Hanford Nuclear Reservation, and it spans Yakima County and Grant County.\n- The Hanford Site is a mostly decommissioned nuclear production complex on the Columbia River in Washington that is operated by the United States federal government.\n- The Hanford Site has also been known as the Hanford Project, Hanford Works, Hanford Engineer Works, and Hanford Nuclear Reservation.\n- Grant County Public Utility District operates the hydroelectric projects Priest Rapids Dam and Wanapum Dam.\n- Rattlesnake Mountain, also called Lalíik in a Native American name meaning \"land above the water,\" is a 3,527-foot windswept treeless sub-alpine ridge overlooking the Hanford nuclear site.",
